WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.440
In 1779, three years
after David Hume died,

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.150
his Dialogues concerning
Natural Religion were published.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.680
In it, a sceptic called Philo
says: if we see a house,

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.980
we conclude that it had a builder.

5
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.040
But does the universe
really resemble a house?

6
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.160
If the world looks designed,
does that point to God,

7
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.380
to many makers, or to nature itself?

8
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.910
In this mission, you'll test
Hume's attack on that analogy,

9
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.710
one point at a time.

10
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.180
Then you'll weigh up whether the design
argument can survive its critics.

11
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.090
Your mission: weigh up what, if anything,

12
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.160
the look of design points to.
